# Remotion Component Development Patterns

## Component Structure
Each component lives in its own folder:
- `index.tsx` — main implementation
- `types.ts` — TypeScript prop interfaces
- `README.md` — component documentation
- `ComponentName.test.tsx` — Jest + React Testing Library tests

## Atomic Design Hierarchy
- **Atoms**: Basic building blocks (`AnimatedText`, `AnimatedCircle`, `ScrollingPage`)
- **Molecules**: Composites (`IntroSection`, `ContentSection`, `OutroSection`, `CaptionPage`)
- **Organisms**: Full compositions (`HelloWorldComposition`, `TransitionsDemo`, `CaptionsDemo`)

## Remotion Hooks
```ts
import { useCurrentFrame, useVideoConfig, interpolate, spring } from 'remotion';
```

For caption components, also `useDelayRender` to hold the render until async data resolves.

## Schemas
Define schemas in `src/index.tsx` next to the `<Composition>` registration. Component prop interfaces should mark all schema-backed fields as **optional** so the FC type satisfies Remotion's `LooseComponentType<Record<string, unknown>>`. Provide defaults inside the component:

```ts
export const MyComp: React.FC<MyCompProps> = ({ title = 'Hello' }) => { ... };
```

## Animation Patterns
- `spring()` — organic motion
- `interpolate()` — frame-driven property transitions (always set `extrapolateLeft`/`extrapolateRight`)
- `useCurrentFrame()` — current frame number
- `useVideoConfig()` — width/height/fps

## Tailwind v4
`className` is allowed on container elements (see `IntroSection` for the canonical migration). Tailwind is wired via `@remotion/tailwind-v4` in both `remotion.config.ts` (Studio) and `render.mjs` (headless).

**Forbidden Tailwind classes**: `transition-*`, `animate-*`, and any other CSS-time-based animation utility. Remotion renders frame-by-frame; CSS transitions don't apply. Animate via `useCurrentFrame()` + `interpolate()`/`spring()` instead. See `.claude/skills/remotion/rules/tailwind.md`.

## Transitions (`@remotion/transitions`)
```ts
import { TransitionSeries, linearTiming } from '@remotion/transitions';
import { fade } from '@remotion/transitions/fade';
import { slide } from '@remotion/transitions/slide';
```

`<TransitionSeries>` shortens total duration by the sum of transition durations because adjacent scenes overlap during transitions. Account for this in the `<Composition>` `durationInFrames` (see `TRANSITIONS_DEMO_DURATION_IN_FRAMES` in [TransitionsDemo/index.tsx](mdc:src/components/organisms/TransitionsDemo/index.tsx)).

## Captions (`@remotion/captions`)
```ts
import { parseSrt, createTikTokStyleCaptions } from '@remotion/captions';
import { staticFile, useDelayRender } from 'remotion';
```

Pattern: fetch the SRT inside `useEffect`, hold the render with `delayRender()`, parse on success and `continueRender()` (or `cancelRender()` on failure). Group tokens with `createTikTokStyleCaptions({ combineTokensWithinMilliseconds })`. Render each page in a `<Sequence>` whose `from` and `durationInFrames` are derived from `page.startMs`. See [CaptionsDemo/index.tsx](mdc:src/components/organisms/CaptionsDemo/index.tsx).

## Testing
Global mocks live in [src/setupTests.ts](mdc:src/setupTests.ts) and cover `useCurrentFrame`, `useVideoConfig`, `interpolate`, `spring`, `staticFile`, `useDelayRender`, `AbsoluteFill`, and `Sequence`. Per-test mocks for `@remotion/transitions` and `@remotion/captions` go inline in the test file (see [TransitionsDemo.test.tsx](mdc:src/components/organisms/TransitionsDemo/TransitionsDemo.test.tsx) and [CaptionsDemo.test.tsx](mdc:src/components/organisms/CaptionsDemo/CaptionsDemo.test.tsx)).

